# Copy to .env next to compose.yaml on all four boxes, the same file on each. PEERS is required unless MENTAT=1: edit
# and uncomment it below. Unset, the other settings take the image's defaults (Dockerfile) and TUNE's (knobs.sh).

# --- the four boxes ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edit these three lines for your boxes, then remove the # from each. They are commented out on purpose: a copy of this
# file never starts the boxes with example addresses (with PEERS unset, the boot stops and says so). With MENTAT=1
# (README.md, "Clustering") leave all three commented out.
# Their 10G LAN addresses, head first. The head serves the API.
#PEERS=<head-lan-ip>,<box2-lan-ip>,<box3-lan-ip>,<box4-lan-ip>
# Each box's ConnectX address on PCIe root 1 (IPS) and PCIe root 2 (IPS2), in PEERS order.
#IPS=<head-root1-ip>,<box2-root1-ip>,<box3-root1-ip>,<box4-root1-ip>
#IPS2=<head-root2-ip>,<box2-root2-ip>,<box3-root2-ip>,<box4-root2-ip>
# Four boxes cabled in a ring without a switch (gr8/docs/DEPLOY.md): list PEERS in cable order, each box's f0 port
# cabled to the next box's f1 port, and leave out IPS and IPS2.
#SHAPE=ring

# --- the knobs (README.md, "Knobs") ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What to prioritize (README.md, "Pick what to prioritize"): speed (the default), context or quality. Each sets
# VARIANT, SESS, CAP, MAX_MODEL_LEN and MTP; speed/context also enable S2_SHARED_WATERFILL=1, and context turns on
# context-parallel KV (knobs.sh). A value set below keeps its value.
#TUNE=speed
# The width manifest of the release: k4.
#VARIANT=k4
# The requests that decode at once: 8.
#SESS=8
# The KV pool in tokens, shared by the sessions, a multiple of 64: 262208 for speed and quality, 2097152 for context.
#CAP=262208
# The longest single request, prompt and output together, at most CAP less the guard rows (and 1,048,576):
# 262144 for speed and quality, 1048576 for context.
#MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
# 0 by default (MTP only; no drafter configured by default).
#DFLASH=0
# 0: the boxes in PEERS. 1: find the other boxes and register the API through the host's mentat daemon, in group GROUP.
#MENTAT=0
#GROUP=gr8-sage-4x
# Text-only is the default. The release includes dense/vision-bf16.safetensors (1.13 GB, untested with this recipe).
# To opt in, set GR8_GLM53F_VISION=1 in EXTRA_ENV on all four boxes:
#EXTRA_ENV="GR8_GLM53F_VISION=1"
# Reply length and tool-call behavior (gr8/KNOBS.md):
#DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS=32768
#DEFAULT_THINK_END_BOOST=
#DEFAULT_THINKING_BUDGET=0
#DEFAULT_PRESENCE_PENALTY=0
#UNDECLARED_TOOL_CALLS=emit

# --- host directories in place of the named volumes, each owned by uid 1000 ------------------------------------------
#MODEL_CACHE_DIR=/srv/sage-4x/cache      # this box's part of the model (~47 GB at TP=4)
#PROMPT_CACHE_DIR=/srv/sage-4x/prompts   # the prompt cache, up to 64 GB (kv-store.yaml)
#GR8_HOME_DIR=/srv/sage-4x/home          # logs and state

# --- the image ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A pinned image in place of latest, e.g. ghcr.io/kindlingai/sage-s2.1-flash-exlr8-4x-spark:sha-<commit>
#IMAGE=

# --- other -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The release, pinned to a Hugging Face commit (https://huggingface.co/<org>/<repo>@<commit>).
# Drop the @<commit> to follow the repo's main.
#MODEL=https://huggingface.co/kindlingai/sage-s2.1-flash-exlr8-k4@e55da4682c090821efcac7f5fb85622cb06d1c54
# Sent only to Hugging Face, for a gated or private repo
#HF_TOKEN=
# Any other gr8 launcher option (gr8/KNOBS.md) works here too, as NAME=VALUE.
